# CrossEngin domain pack: world history milestones (v1)
#
# ~80 atoms + ~60 implications covering broadly-consensus historical
# milestones from antiquity through the 20th century. Deliberately
# focused on well-documented, high-consensus events (dates + primary
# actors + first-order consequences); avoids interpretive claims where
# scholars actively disagree.
#
# Ontological is-a edges (an event IS a historical_event; a war IS a
# conflict) get FORMAL strength. Causal claims ("industrial_revolution
# caused urbanization") stay EMPIRICAL because historical causation is
# subject to reinterpretation.
#
# Ingest via:
#   /ingest cerec data/packs/world_history.cerec history \
#           src:pack:world_history:v1

KG history
SRC src:pack:world_history:v1

# ============================================================================
# 1. Root ontology
# ============================================================================

ATOM historical_event 3 950
ATOM war 3 950
ATOM revolution 3 950
ATOM treaty 3 950
ATOM invention 3 950
ATOM discovery 3 950
ATOM civilization 3 950
ATOM person 3 950

IMP war historical_event FORMAL
IMP revolution historical_event FORMAL
IMP treaty historical_event FORMAL
IMP invention historical_event FORMAL
IMP discovery historical_event FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 2. Ancient civilizations
# ============================================================================

ATOM ancient_egypt 3 900
ATOM ancient_greece 3 950
ATOM roman_empire 3 950
ATOM han_dynasty 3 900
ATOM maurya_empire 3 900
ATOM mesopotamia 3 950

IMP ancient_egypt civilization FORMAL
IMP ancient_greece civilization FORMAL
IMP roman_empire civilization FORMAL
IMP han_dynasty civilization FORMAL
IMP maurya_empire civilization FORMAL
IMP mesopotamia civilization FORMAL

ATOM cuneiform 1 900
ATOM alphabet 1 900
IMP cuneiform invention EMPIRICAL
IMP alphabet invention EMPIRICAL
IMP mesopotamia cuneiform EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 3. Middle ages / medieval
# ============================================================================

ATOM printing_press_1440 1 950
ATOM gutenberg 1 950
IMP printing_press_1440 invention FORMAL
IMP gutenberg person FORMAL
IMP gutenberg printing_press_1440 EMPIRICAL

ATOM black_death_1347 1 950
IMP black_death_1347 historical_event FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 4. Age of exploration + scientific revolution
# ============================================================================

ATOM columbus_1492 1 950
ATOM columbus 1 950
IMP columbus person FORMAL
IMP columbus columbus_1492 EMPIRICAL
IMP columbus_1492 historical_event FORMAL

ATOM copernicus 1 950
ATOM heliocentric_model 1 950
IMP copernicus person FORMAL
IMP heliocentric_model discovery FORMAL
IMP copernicus heliocentric_model EMPIRICAL

ATOM newton 1 950
ATOM principia_1687 1 950
ATOM law_of_gravitation 3 950
IMP newton person FORMAL
IMP principia_1687 historical_event FORMAL
IMP law_of_gravitation discovery FORMAL
IMP newton principia_1687 EMPIRICAL
IMP newton law_of_gravitation EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 5. Modern era: revolutions and industrial change
# ============================================================================

ATOM american_revolution 1 950
ATOM us_independence_1776 1 950
IMP american_revolution revolution FORMAL
IMP us_independence_1776 historical_event FORMAL

ATOM french_revolution 1 950
ATOM french_revolution_1789 1 950
IMP french_revolution revolution FORMAL
IMP french_revolution_1789 historical_event FORMAL

ATOM industrial_revolution 1 950
ATOM steam_engine 1 950
ATOM urbanization 3 900
IMP industrial_revolution historical_event FORMAL
IMP steam_engine invention FORMAL
IMP industrial_revolution steam_engine EMPIRICAL
IMP industrial_revolution urbanization EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 6. 20th century milestones
# ============================================================================

ATOM world_war_1 1 950
ATOM world_war_2 1 950
ATOM treaty_of_versailles 1 900
IMP world_war_1 war FORMAL
IMP world_war_2 war FORMAL
IMP treaty_of_versailles treaty FORMAL
IMP world_war_1 treaty_of_versailles EMPIRICAL

ATOM einstein 1 950
ATOM general_relativity 1 950
IMP einstein person FORMAL
IMP general_relativity discovery FORMAL
IMP einstein general_relativity EMPIRICAL

ATOM moon_landing_1969 1 950
ATOM apollo_11 1 950
IMP moon_landing_1969 historical_event FORMAL
IMP apollo_11 moon_landing_1969 EMPIRICAL

ATOM internet 1 950
ATOM tim_berners_lee 1 900
ATOM world_wide_web 1 950
IMP internet invention FORMAL
IMP world_wide_web invention FORMAL
IMP tim_berners_lee person FORMAL
IMP tim_berners_lee world_wide_web EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 7. Cross-source citations
# ============================================================================

CITE src:pack:world_history:v1 src:paper:doi:britannica-world-history supports
CITE src:pack:world_history:v1 src:paper:doi:cambridge-history-of-modern-world extends
CITE src:pack:world_history:v1 src:pack:physics:v1 supports

# ============================================================================
# 8. Reinforcing observations for the highest-confidence claims
# ============================================================================

OBS printing_press_1440 +1 1000
OBS moon_landing_1969 +1 1000
OBS world_war_2 +1 1000
OBS newton +1 1000
